Several questions, really. However, if you are talking about booting 
from paper tape, you either have to write your own boot loader, or you 
need to hook the paper tape reader (or simulator) to the console port 
(assuming the console port can be accessed, and that you have a boot 
prom that supports paper tape from an ASR33.
If you want to access the paper tape from the booted OS, then you need a 
device driver for the ASR33, and then the usual procedure applies. Hook 
to console port, and so on... :-)
But if you want to talk more about this, we can do it privately.

> But, back to the topic at hand...
> 
